<title>USA: USFreightways operating ratio improves.</title>
<headline>USFreightways operating ratio improves.</headline>
<dateline>ROSEMONT, Ill. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USFreightways Corp said Friday the operating ratio of its regional trucking group improved by two percentage points to 92 percent in the second quarter compared with a year earlier.</p>
<p>Earlier, USFreightways reported earnings for the second quarter of $0.56 a share, up from $0.37 a year ago. The company attributed the earnings improvement to a strong U.S. economy, stable pricing environment and cost reduction.</p>
<p>&quot;The outlook for the balance of 1997 is positive and we expect to continue to see an improvement in our profitability, assuming no material change in the stable pricing environment and level of economic activity,&quot; Cam Carruth, president, said in a statement.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
